Z||000000||Philphine||05-01-2001||12:44 PM||||<BR>i know i spelled coloume wrong. i'm still looking at the 6000 ste that is at the dav lot near me for a brake parts sourse. remember it also has a radio controlling steering wheel. <P>my '87 is going to need a steering coloume and i'm just wondering if it might be compatible. <P>i'm in no hurry to do the brake job (for a longer term project) so i'm just watching the car to see if it gets cheap enough to be worth getting (the last one i got there, my cheap thrill fiero, they sold to me for the price they would have sold it to the junk yard for), and in the meantime trying to find out what all i can use off it to justify getting it.<P>thanks for any help. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfixit58||05-01-2001||01:50 PM||||I just pulled a steering column apart for an 89 Firebird GTA. It, too, had the radio controller on the steering wheel. I don't think the steering columns will interchange, although a side-by-side comparison would be needed to be sure. <P>The good news is all the internal components will interchange. The radio controls are part of the turn signal cam and harness. If you replace your harness with the one from the 6000 and use it's steering wheel, it'll work. That is, of course, if you also using the 6000 radio (or an aftermarket equivalent.<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
